		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=5006&amp;p=36435#p36435"><![CDATA[
I found that the chip in this machine is the same as the one in the 1701—both contain identical main control chips, HR-6000 chips, and an AT1846S. However, this machine only has one encoder. The front panel layout is the same as the TYT-UV380.<br><br>Porting the GD77 firmware to it will turn this into an even more fun walkie-talkie!<br><img src="https://github.com/cnt7/7-S-image/blob/main/IMG_9357.JPG?raw=FALSE" class="postimage" alt="Image"><br><img src="https://github.com/cnt7/7-S-image/blob/main/IMG_9355.JPG?raw=FALSE" class="postimage" alt="Image"><br><img src="https://github.com/cnt7/7-S-image/blob/main/IMG_9353.JPG?raw=FALSE" class="postimage" alt="Image"><p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=8338">BI1GLL</a> — Tue Mar 25, 2025 6:45 am</p><hr />
